=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/CommandHistory (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/CommandHistory   kind=page   web route=/command-history
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/CommandHistoryPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300); maui-windows workload installed;
              full WinUI Release build of the solution succeeds — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the data feed / generated-client adapter, also headless),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable observable state holder, the established testable
  pattern — see TimelinePageViewModel / ApiLogsPageViewModel) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated
  prompt's idealized "CommandHistoryPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/System" is mapped onto these
  real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("CommandHistory").
- Namespace: TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (NOT ".System" — a sibling namespace segment literally named
  "System" shadows global::System for every other FeatureViews.* file that writes an inline System.* name, which
  broke the whole app compile; "SystemOps" mirrors the route's RouteGroup.SystemOps and is collision-free).
- Data sources (manifest: useCommandHistory → GET /vehicles/{vehicleId}/commands/history [limit]): bound through an
  injected ICommandHistoryFeed (P1/S8 seam). The generated-client-backed CommandHistoryClientFeed (ADR-004) reads
  the web page's two sources — the useSelectedVehicle fleet list (generated op get_api_v1_vehicles) and the
  per-vehicle log (op get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_commands_history with the snake_case limit=200 query the web
  useCommandHistory hook requests). Default EmptyCommandHistoryFeed resolves the empty state with no HTTP. The
  view never performs HTTP. Both generated op ids verified present in Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs.
- Stats (Commands-24h / Success-Rate / Most-Used / Last-Sent), client-side status+search filtering and the 25-row
  pagination are computed in CommandHistoryProjection exactly as the web useMemo blocks do, including the
  COMMAND_LABELS friendly-name map + formatCommandName fallback and the params/error buildSubtitle. Timestamps
  format through the shared DateTimeFormatting port; the timeline renders on the W3 TsTimeline (severity-coloured
  markers). No charts / maps in this unit (manifest declares 0 / 0).
- All 18 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (translation.commandHistory.* +
  translation.filter.pending); the surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names
  (no new catalog rows required). The "{0} commands" showing-count + "{rate}%" use the .resw {0} placeholders.
- Three false-positive "Placeholder" matches (the required commandHistory.searchPlaceholder key + its projected
  field/Hint) carry the repo's // parity:allow <reason> opt-out, the same mechanism TsSelect/TsInput use for the
  WinUI PlaceholderText API. No stubs, no TODO/FIXME, no "Coming soon" (ADR-011).

